(4771127, 686697, 9462, '<td valign="top">Hi Jane,<br/>My choice for blue was DQ''d and you were my 2nd choice.<br/>Your image feels so natural and complete<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=670650" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/5000-9999/9462/120/670650.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/5000-9999/9462/120/670650.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/5000-9999/9462/120/670650.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Hi Jane,My choice for blue was DQ''d and you were my 2nd choice.Your image feels so natural and complete', '2008-06-16 12:50:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4771177, 686996, 61222, '<td valign="top">I was hoping this would do better. But my lighting was not the best and it was hot and my husband was wore out from working all day. <br/>I feel so sad for the loss of this fine young man and and feel sad for all that are left behind. My prayers and thoughts our with you all. I know words can''t make the pain go away. These are the last 3 verses of a cowboy poem I found on the internet called "Tribute To A Cowboy" I thought they were fitting.<br/> <br/>The only comfort I have found<br/>That puts my grief to rest<br/>Is that God only takes the top hands<br/>Because His crew''s the very best<br/> <br/>We still cry and we sure miss you<br/>And all the things that might have been<br/>But God needed one more cowboy<br/>And He felt you''d fit right in<br/> <br/>So He sent down all His ranch hands<br/>An extra horse stood at their side<br/>Then he softly whispered to you<br/>"Saddle up, my friend, let''s ride"<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-06-16 12:38:40.</i></td>', 'I was hoping this would do better. But my lighting was not the best and it was hot and my husband was wore out from working all day. I feel so sad for the loss of this fine young man and and feel sad for all that are left behind. My prayers and thoughts our with you all. I know words can''t make the pain go away. These are the last 3 verses of a cowboy poem I found on the internet called "Tribute To A Cowboy" I thought they were fitting. The only comfort I have foundThat puts my grief to restIs that God only takes the top handsBecause His crew''s the very best We still cry and we sure miss youAnd all the things that might have beenBut God needed one more cowboyAnd He felt you''d fit right in So He sent down all His ranch handsAn extra horse stood at their sideThen he softly whispered to you"Saddle up, my friend, let''s ride"', '2008-06-16 13:24:06.000000', '2008-06-16 13:38:40.000000', 0),
(4771246, 686774, 87808, '<td valign="top">Well done!!! Love the shot and your husband is still as good looking as always!!!</td>', 'Well done!!! Love the shot and your husband is still as good looking as always!!!', '2008-06-16 14:04:48.000000', NULL, 0),
